# Repo-root build context exclusions.
#
# This file applies ONLY when the build context is the repository root. Each
# component's own image (portals/ai-workspace, platform-api, gateway/*, ...) builds
# from its own directory and reads its own .dockerignore instead — Docker reads only
# the .dockerignore at a context's root, never a nested one.
#
# The case this exists for is a build that binds the whole repo as a context, which
# is how downstream cloud wrappers source an unreleased portal — apim-saas's
# apip-ai-workspace image takes `--build-context api-platform-local=<this repo>` for
# local development. Without these two entries BuildKit transfers ~1.4GB of a typical
# working tree, nearly all of it files no build reads.
#
# Deliberately minimal: only things that are regenerated inside every image that
# needs them, so no build can be broken by their absence. Component-specific
# exclusions belong in that component's own .dockerignore, not here.

# Reinstalled inside the image by npm ci / npm install (~590MB here, and built for
# the developer's platform rather than the image's linux/*).
**/node_modules

# Repository history (~630MB). No Dockerfile in this repo reads it: the builds that
# stamp a commit take it as a build ARG (GIT_COMMIT) rather than shelling out to git.
.git
